index=entra sourcetype="azure:loganalytics:auditlogs" LoggedByService="PIM" earliest=-1h latest=now
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` Detection (SPL): Privileged Identity Management (PIM) activation            ```
```                  (PIM for Groups + PIM for roles)                           ```
``` Lab:             Contoso Health Identity Platform - Splunk second SIEM        ```
``` KQL twin:        lab/kql/pim-activation.kql (same logic/window/columns)       ```
``` -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` STAND-IN: runs on the Splunk Enterprise 60-day TRIAL (replaces production   ```
``` Splunk) over Entra logs REPLAYED from Log Analytics by                      ```
``` lab/splunk/ingest-from-loganalytics.sh (replaces the Splunk Add-on for      ```
``` Microsoft Azure / Event Hub streaming). Base search is line 1 on purpose:   ```
``` a comment before the first command breaks a Splunk search.                  ```
```                                                                            ```
``` WHAT IT CATCHES                                                             ```
```   A just-in-time elevation that actually COMPLETED: an eligible member of  ```
```   Privileged-IAM-Admins activating (PIM for Groups), or a direct PIM role  ```
```   activation. Requests/approvals are not matched - only the grant.         ```
```   HighValue=true marks the role-bearing group or a Tier-0/1 role.          ```
```                                                                            ```
``` KQL -> SPL TRANSLATION                                                      ```
```   where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)           -> earliest=-1h latest=now        ```
```   LoggedByService == PIM (case-SENSITIVE) -> base-search pre-filter (case-  ```
```                                              insensitive) + where ==        ```
```   Category in (GroupManagement, RoleManagement) -> where in(Category, ...)  ```
```                                              (both case-sensitive)          ```
```   ActivityDisplayName has PIM activation  ```
```     and has completed (has = whole-term, case-insensitive)                 ```
```                                           -> where match(..., (?i) term     ```
```                                              bounded by start/end or a non- ```
```                                              alphanumeric char - the KQL    ```
```                                              term boundary; no backslash    ```
```                                              escapes to survive eval quoting) ```
```   tostring(InitiatedBy.user.*)            -> spath path=InitiatedBy.user.*  ```
```   mv-apply tr = TargetResources on (                                       ```
```     summarize take_anyif(displayName, type == Group / Role))               ```
```                                           -> spath path=TargetResources{}   ```
```                                              + mvfilter(type == Group/Role) ```
```                                              + displayName of the 1st match ```
```                                              (picked by TYPE, never index)  ```
```   iff(isnotempty(TargetGroup), ...)       -> eval if(non-empty, ...)        ```
```   ElevatedTo in (high-value list)         -> in() - case-sensitive, as KQL  ```
```   AdditionalDetails (raw dynamic bag)     -> spath path=AdditionalDetails{} ```
```                                              (one key/value JSON per value) ```
```   project ... | sort by TimeGenerated desc -> sort 0 - _time | table ...    ```
``` VERIFY (same as the KQL): after the first real activation, copy the exact  ```
``` ActivityDisplayName strings from the events - Microsoft has renamed PIM    ```
``` activity strings before. verify: eval spath() on each TargetResources{}    ```
``` element (its JSON text); mvfilter itself is documented.                     ```
```                                                                            ```
``` SCHEDULE: mirrors the Sentinel rule (lab/terraform/modules/monitoring):     ```
``` PT5M / PT1H, severity Medium, trigger > 0 rows, 1 h grouping by Account +   ```
``` IP entities (Actor, ActorIp).                                               ```
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` 2026-11-07 (review findings B5, B6): the group is read from type Group   ```
``` OR a named type Other entry (the shape the tenant really logs), and Tier 0 ```
``` is decided by name (Tier-0 roles, PIM-Tier0-*, PIM-AWS-Lab-Admins,        ```
``` Privileged-IAM-Admins). DIFFERENCE from the KQL twin, stated plainly: no   ```
``` object-id match, no off-hours and no new-IP leg here (no Splunk lookup for ```
``` the ids, no sign-in history join), so Severity is Medium for Tier 0 and    ```
``` Informational otherwise, and OffHours / NewIp read "not computed".        ```
``` @stanza Contoso - PIM activation (just-in-time elevation) ```
``` @conf description = A PIM for Groups / PIM for roles activation completed. Expected for approved changes; every one is reviewed. KQL twin: lab/kql/pim-activation.kql ```
``` @conf disabled = 0 ```
``` @conf enableSched = 1 ```
``` @conf cron_schedule = */5 * * * * ```
``` @conf dispatch.earliest_time = -1h ```
``` @conf dispatch.latest_time = now ```
``` @conf counttype = number of events ```
``` @conf relation = greater than ```
``` @conf quantity = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.track = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.severity = 4 ```
``` @conf alert.expires = 7d ```
``` @conf alert.digest_mode = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.fields = Actor,ActorIp ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.period = 1h ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_app = search ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_view = search ```
| where LoggedByService=="PIM" AND in(Category, "GroupManagement", "RoleManagement")
| where match(ActivityDisplayName, "(?i)(^|[^A-Za-z0-9])PIM activation($|[^A-Za-z0-9])") AND match(ActivityDisplayName, "(?i)(^|[^A-Za-z0-9])completed($|[^A-Za-z0-9])")
| spath path=InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName output=Actor
| spath path=InitiatedBy.user.id output=ActorObjectId
| spath path=InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress output=ActorIp
| spath path=TargetResources{} output=TR
| eval TRGroup=mvfilter(spath(TR, "type")=="Group" OR (spath(TR, "type")=="Other" AND spath(TR, "displayName")!=""))
| eval TRRole=mvfilter(spath(TR, "type")=="Role")
| eval TRGroup1=mvindex(TRGroup, 0)
| eval TRRole1=mvindex(TRRole, 0)
| eval TargetGroup=spath(TRGroup1, "displayName")
| eval TargetRole=spath(TRRole1, "displayName")
| eval HasGroup=if(isnotnull(TargetGroup) AND TargetGroup!="", 1, 0)
| eval ElevatedTo=if(HasGroup==1, TargetGroup, TargetRole)
| eval ElevationType=if(HasGroup==1, "PIM for Groups", "PIM for roles")
| eval Tier0By=if(isnotnull(ElevatedTo) AND (in(ElevatedTo, "Global Administrator", "Privileged Role Administrator", "Privileged Authentication Administrator", "Security Administrator", "Conditional Access Administrator", "Application Administrator", "Cloud Application Administrator", "Hybrid Identity Administrator", "Authentication Policy Administrator", "Privileged-IAM-Admins", "PIM-AWS-Lab-Admins") OR like(ElevatedTo, "PIM-Tier0-%")), "name", "")
| eval HighValue=if(Tier0By!="", "true", "false")
| eval OffHours="not computed", NewIp="not computed"
| eval Severity=if(HighValue=="true", "Medium", "Informational")
| spath path=AdditionalDetails{} output=AdditionalDetails
| sort 0 - _time
| table TimeGenerated, Actor, ActorObjectId, ActorIp, ElevationType, ElevatedTo, HighValue, Tier0By, OffHours, NewIp, Severity, Result, ActivityDisplayName, CorrelationId, AdditionalDetails
